terval edit from user-supplied Classic Break Pack files. Recording and composition rights remain with their respective rights holders.","source":"User-supplied Classic Break Pack","sourceAudio":null,"slotSHA256":"e28d614f5a125c4ec480e0d1140f951cec7e8252e932cf402ede1aa4288a29e3","status":"clearance-not-documented","firmwareRedistributionPermission":null,"licenseDocument":null,"sourceFiles":[{"name":"lyncollins_think_1.wav","sha256":"940003936ea19125942ca953e2910ce666a6eb7d694bd159da826350af87fd15","rate":44100,"frames":93761,"source_beats":4},{"name":"lyncollins_think_2.wav","sha256":"0f2517a607ca16598fdd67336c90df211d7e958a6b23cb481df331efc9939eec","rate":44100,"frames":92698,"source_beats":4}],"edit":"Think drums / two complementary assembled bars","previousSlotSHA256":"a3d0ec9f0bc0e56310d94024f5530caf255303a2aac7f95748815596a6285a9d","processing":"Two complementary drums-only bars; offline level matching with bounded peak control and zero loop endpoints.","levelMatch":{"source_slot_sha256":"a3d0ec9f0bc0e56310d94024f5530caf255303a2aac7f95748815596a6285a9d","slot_sha256":"e28d614f5a125c4ec480e0d1140f951cec7e8252e932cf402ede1aa4288a29e3","gain_db":9.0,"max_peak_attenuation_db":9.674933884213901,"amen_rms":0.19167527341802548,"think_before_rms":0.08451214112044729,"think_after_rms":0.15193656195334387,"rms_difference_db":-2.0180759309055034,"true_peak_dbfs":-1.3702431050771096,"clipped_samples":0,"frames":48000,"seam_jump_pcm16":0,"runtime_cpu_cost_added":0}}],"references":["https://github.com/ejtb76/amenity#third-party-audio","https://rhythm-lab.com/breakbeats/","https://www.copyright.gov/music-modernization/educational-materials/Sampling-Interpolations-Beat-Stores-and-More-An-Introduction-for-Musicians-Using-Preexisting.pdf"],"distributionDecision":{"requestedBy":"Jazzy Rhythmer","date":"2026-11-06","includeOriginalRecordings":true,"ownerDirectedPublicDistribution":true,"permissionEvidenceProvided":false,"reason":"Owner explicitly requests redistribution of Amen and Think with credits, a rights acknowledgement and user-replaceable sample banks. The request is not a rights-holder license."}},"audioNotice":"RHYTHMER / THIRD-PARTY AUDIO \u2014 BUNDLED THIRD-PARTY RECORDINGS\n\nA / AMEN \u2014 \"Amen, Brother\", The Winstons (1969).\nDrums: Gregory C. Coleman. Amenity credits composition to Richard L. Spencer.\nSource: https://github.com/ejtb76/amenity/tree/main/assets/third-party/amen\nB / THINK \u2014 \"Think (About It)\", Lyn Collins.\nSource: user-supplied Classic Break Pack, lyncollins_think_1.wav and\nlyncollins_think_2.wav. Drum intervals assembled into two complementary bars;\npitched tail/carry-in intervals excluded. Original files retained by the owner.\n\nBoth: mono PCM12 / 16 kHz / two bars at 160 BPM / 3 seconds. Prepared\nwith cropping, repitch/resampling, level adjustment and endpoint fades.\nThese recordings are NOT covered by Rhythmer's software license. Rights\nremain with the respective recording and composition rights holders.\nNo permission for public firmware/sample redistribution or musical releases\nhas been documented for these copies. Credits and notices do not grant it.\nThe project owner directs public distribution with these credits. This\ndecision is not rights-holder permission, and does not clear any user use.\n\nRecording/composition permissions may be needed for distributing\nthese recordings as firmware/sample assets, or replace/omit them. A license\nallowing samples in a finished song may not allow a redistributable sample bank.\nSee audio-rights.json for source URLs, exact slot hashes and clearance status.\n"}
